body:
This PR adds `setCommandSchema()`, an API which lets an app embedding `<perspective-viewer>` add its own commands to the right-click menu, with click context.

```javascript
viewer.setCommandSchema((context) => {
      const id = context.hit?.row.security_id;
      return {
            commands: id == null ? [] : [{
                  kind: "Command",
                  key: "open-ticket",
                  label: `Open Ticket (${id})`,
            }],
      };
});

viewer.addEventListener("perspective-command", (event) => {
      const { key, context } = event.detail;
      if (key === "open-ticket") {
            openOrderTicket(context.hit.row.security_id, context.point);
      }
});
```

- `setCommandSchema()` takes a synchronous function from a context (panel, table, plugin, view config, click point, and the `hit` under the cursor) to a list of `Command` / `Group` entries, shaped like `plugin_config_schema`.
- Picking a command fires `perspective-command` with its `key` and the same context.
- Plugins gain three optional methods: `hit_test(x, y)`, plus `command_schema()` / `execute_command()` to offer commands of their own. Datagrid and charts implement `hit_test`.
- React: `commandSchema` and `onCommand` props.
- With no schema set, the right-click path is unchanged.
